        {
          "id": "SP_PANAGROLAIMUS_LEPERISINI_MASSEY_1974",
          "name": "Panagrolaimus leperisini Massey, 1974",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Panagrolaimus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Panagrolaimus. Leperisini was first described in the U. S. A. as an associate of the bark beetle Leperisinus aculeatus (Say) in green ash (Fraxinus pennsylvanica Marshall) (Massey 1974). This is the only known report of this species. Measurements. See table 5. Description. Female (n = 2): Habitus slightly curved ventrally. Cuticle moderately annulated, annule width 2 µm at midbody. Fine longitudinal striations. Lateral field with three incisures, about one-seventh of corresponding body width. Lips rounded, each bearing one small seta (Fig. 7 A – B). Six labial and four cephalic setae. Stoma 11 – 12 µm in length. Cheilostom distinct, 3 µm in length, gymnostom 4 – 5 µm and stegostom 3 µm long. Meso-, meta- and telorhabdions fused (Fig. 7 A – B). Metarhabdions bearing prominent dorsal tooth (Fig. 7 A – B). Corpus twice the isthmus length (Fig. 7 A – B). Corpus-isthmus junction distinct, isthmus narrower than corpus (Fig. 7 A – B). Nerve ring situated at mid-isthmus, 124 – 130 µm from anterior end. Basal bulb ovoid with well-developed valves (Fig. 7 A – B). Excretory pore slightly posterior to nerve ring, passing through hemizonid (Fig. 7 A – B). Cardia distinct, 6 µm in length. Vulva at 56 %, vulval lips protruding (Fig. 7 C). Vagina one-third of corresponding body width, directed anteriorly. Reproductive system monodelphic-prodelphic (Fig. 7 C). Ovary reflexed. Post-vulval uterine sac short, less than half the corresponding body width (Fig. 7 C).",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9437591"
        },
